    "q-80371": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80371",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $K$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}b & 1 \\\\ 0 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}b & 1 \\\\ 0 & c\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get  $a=-5,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
